  "notes": "Behavior-change (migration) reference: the developer-facing surface is the delta in value resolution for three long-shipped properties, not new syntax. The border-width resolved-value carve-out (getComputedStyle still 0px under none/hidden) is the single most important contract on the page; it is sourced verbatim from css-backgrounds-3 ED and the ChromeStatus compat assessment, and was the factual error fixed in this upgrade (the previous page revision claimed getComputedStyle().borderWidth reads the authored value in Chrome 147+, which is wrong)."
